 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-14: C2ME idea 1: chunk meshing on the worker threads (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +2 tests `chunks::tests::{worker_mesh_is_the_in_place_mesh, mesh_results_land_and_an_edit_queues_the_next_job}`, not run). Source: RelativityMC/C2ME-fabric (concurrent chunk management); a literal port makes no sense (its ~25 modules are Mixins into modern vanilla classes that b1.7.3 does not have), so only its ideas are taken, one per session: this one is the scheduler (`c2me-rewrites-chunk-system`: chunk work off the main thread, nearest first). Still open from that audit: save writes on an I/O thread (`rewrites-chunkio`), populate + light on the workers, bit-exact noise speedups (`opts-math` / `worldgen`).
+    - Root cause of the hitches left after the FPS fix: `ChunkManager::mesh_pending` ran `mesh::build_split_tinted` + `by_section` + the climate sampling for the tints on the render thread. Now `Job` (`Gen` | `Mesh`) shares the workers' one queue; `MeshJob` carries a copy of the chunk and its +X / -X / +Z / -Z neighbours (blocks, metadata, light), the worker runs `build_job` with its own `WorldChunkManager`, and `mesh_pending` only uploads what came back (`Built` -> `Mesh`, buffer creation needs the device) and queues new jobs nearest first. One job per chunk at a time (`meshing`), at most `2 x workers` out; `MESH_PER_FRAME` / `CHUNK_WORK_BUDGET` now cap the uploads.
+    - Staleness: `Entry.meshed` is set when the job is queued and cleared by every edit (`put_region`, `mark_dirty`, `set_sky_sub`: unchanged), so an edit during a job leaves the chunk due another one. A result for a chunk edited meanwhile is still shown (it is newer than the mesh it replaces, and a chunk that keeps changing, flowing water, would starve otherwise); only one for an unloaded chunk is dropped.
+    - ponytail: the copy is ~0.4 MB per job (upgrade: `Arc` chunk arrays + `Arc::make_mut`, no copy); an edit shows after a job round trip (queue + build + upload, a frame or a few), not in the same frame as before; jobs share the FIFO with generation (`2 x workers` of each out at most), no priority beyond nearest-first queuing. UNVERIFIED on a device: the cost of the copy, whether 1-2 workers keep up with fast walking (levers: `workers` and `max_meshing` in `ChunkManager::new`).
 - 2026-10-14: UI: inventory icons as big as the hotbar's, white "Crafting" label, crafting block moved left (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +1 test `hud::tests::outlined_text_is_white_over_a_thin_black_rim`, not run; `slots_sit_on_the_panels_frames` covers the move, its Python twin passed on the new `containers.rgba`).
     - Icon size, root cause in `lib.rs` `build_hud`: the hotbar draws its icon 14 of 16 hotbar units (`hw / 20` px a unit) and the screens drew it 16 of 16 PANEL units (`k` px a unit), two different px sizes (63.8 vs 52.9 px at 1604 x 720). The screen's `slot` closure and the picked-up stack now pass `icon_fill = 14 * hotbar_cell / 20 / (16 * k)` to `push_stack`, so every container screen (inventory, workbench, furnace, chest, dispenser) shows the hotbar's size. The count and the wear bar keep their 16-unit box.
     - "Crafting": `HudPipeline::push_text_outlined` (white, 8 black copies `(k * 0.3).max(1)` px round it, no shadow) draws it on the inventory and the workbench; `push_text` and it share `push_glyphs`. The other labels are unchanged (0x404040 + shadow).
